README ■
============

Connect a plain text file with zero markup in to *skvto* and it will output a book-like UI with bells and whistles such as audiobook, chapters, common novel page design. *skvto* also has an editor that allows you to edit your story inline and saves the changes "in the sky cloud".

>check-in README $
@ The Repo

* * *

ORDER OF INITIAL APP SETUP ■
============

    - sktoReader init
        - skvto init
            - add Bells
                - Turn on Notifications
                - Turn on Check-in Fades
            - add Editor
        - setup new page
            - create Title squares
            - get the data, build the blocks
            - fill reader with the blocks
            - add Bells events
        - Set up nav, URL
        - ... user is now in charge ...

* * *

BLOCKS ■
============

    - pre
    - vars
    - h1
    - boxes
    - breaks
    - short breaks
    - em
    - check-ins

* * *

BELLS ■
============

    - play, pause, edit switch
    - check-in fades
    - editor
    - read text
    - notifications
    - swipe nav (TODO: put behind the Bells flag)

